{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "noise": "N2"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 130, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 4 absent, node 3 depends only on edges 3 and 5, so removing edge 3 risks disconnecting or severely bottlenecking the output (e.g. -78/-66/-37 when edges 4 and 5 are both none)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 5 absent, removing the direct edge 0->3 leaves only the path through edge 4, or no path at all, which causes large consistent accuracy drops."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without the direct edge 0->3, information must flow through node 1 or node 2, so cutting edge 0 often disconnects the cell (e.g. -78/-67/-23)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Removing a parameter-free skip on edge 0 in skip-heavy cells breaks the degenerate all-identity collapse, whereas removing a convolution loses capacity."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Deleting a skip on edge 5 in skip-dominated cells gives large gains (+42/+37/+8), while deleting a conv on edge 5 consistently hurts."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Adding another identity path to output in a cell already full of skips worsens the skip collapse (-28/-23/-2), while in conv cells the residual skip helps."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a 3x3 conv to a skip-heavy cell supplies badly needed learnable capacity, giving far larger gains than in already conv-rich cells."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "When downstream edges are parameter-free skips, a conv on edge 0 adds most of the cell's learnable computation (gains of +43 to +49 on CIFAR-10), unlike in conv-dominated cells."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Pooling-only cells have no learnable parameters, so adding a 3x3 conv on edge 5 yields very large improvements (+38/+41/+8) compared with conv-based parents."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "In skip-based cells a conv on the internal edge 1->2 adds rare learnable depth (+5/+14/+10), whereas in conv-rich cells it is redundant and near-neutral."}], "tok": 17324, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "none"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [3, "none"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "none"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none"], [3, "none"]], [["skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect"], [3, "none"]], [["skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "none"], [3, "none"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "none"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none"], [3, "none"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [5, "n